<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William I, Duke of Jülich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1299–1361</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as William V, Count of Jülich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William I, Duke of Jülich, ruled Jülich as Count William V from 1328. An ally of Emperor Louis IV and brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a>, he was made a margrave in 1336 and raised to duke by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Emperor Charles IV</a> in 1356. His reign made Jülich one of the leading territories of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>.</p></div>
